[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3652150807","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/114021#issuecomment-3652150807","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/114021","id":3652150807,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7Zr2YX","user":{"login":"fire","id":32321,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyMzIx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/32321?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire","html_url":"https://github.com/fire","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-12-14T21:18:24Z","updated_at":"2025-12-14T21:18:24Z","body":"Similar to reasoning to avoiding palettes colors in images, I would think that adding a mode that makes quality worse for a PBR engine would be weird.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3652150807/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3652279914","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/114021#issuecomment-3652279914","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/114021","id":3652279914,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7ZsV5q","user":{"login":"shittyprogrammer445","id":96263419,"node_id":"U_kgDOBbzc-w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96263419?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/shittyprogrammer445","html_url":"https://github.com/shittyprogrammer445","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shittyprogrammer445/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shittyprogrammer445/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shittyprogrammer445/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shittyprogrammer445/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shittyprogrammer445/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shittyprogrammer445/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shittyprogrammer445/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shittyprogrammer445/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shittyprogrammer445/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-12-14T22:12:48Z","updated_at":"2025-12-14T22:12:48Z","body":"that's a fair point, however i could say the same thing about per-vertex or lambert lighting. unless i am mistaken and there are real uses for these, they would both result in worse quality than standard pbr.","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3652279914/reactions","total_count":3,"+1":3,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3652356049","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/114021#issuecomment-3652356049","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/114021","id":3652356049,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7ZsofR","user":{"login":"LunaCapra","id":50772474,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUwNzcyNDc0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/50772474?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/LunaCapra","html_url":"https://github.com/LunaCapra","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LunaCapra/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LunaCapra/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LunaCapra/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LunaCapra/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LunaCapra/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LunaCapra/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LunaCapra/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LunaCapra/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LunaCapra/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-12-14T23:05:18Z","updated_at":"2025-12-14T23:05:18Z","body":"> that's a fair point, however i could say the same thing about per-vertex or lambert lighting. unless i am mistaken and there are real uses for these, they would both result in worse quality than standard pbr.\r\n\r\nIn my experience per-vertex shading and lambert diffuse are commonly used \"good enough\" modes that are cheaper to compute, especially for particles/alpha materials that fill the screen\r\nI haven't seen a reason to use affine texture mapping other than emulating an old aesthetic","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3652356049/reactions","total_count":3,"+1":3,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3655013768","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/114021#issuecomment-3655013768","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/114021","id":3655013768,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7Z2xWI","user":{"login":"JekSun97","id":130399274,"node_id":"U_kgDOB8W8Kg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/130399274?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/JekSun97","html_url":"https://github.com/JekSun97","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JekSun97/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JekSun97/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JekSun97/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JekSun97/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JekSun97/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JekSun97/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JekSun97/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JekSun97/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JekSun97/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-12-15T10:57:32Z","updated_at":"2025-12-15T10:57:32Z","body":"> Similar to reasoning to avoiding palettes colors in images, I would think that adding a mode that makes quality worse for a PBR engine would be weird.\r\n\r\nAdding vertex lighting is also considered a rendering degradation, but this did not prevent it from becoming part of Godot.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3655013768/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":1,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3655490172","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/114021#issuecomment-3655490172","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/114021","id":3655490172,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7Z4lp8","user":{"login":"fire","id":32321,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyMzIx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/32321?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire","html_url":"https://github.com/fire","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-12-15T12:55:31Z","updated_at":"2025-12-15T12:55:31Z","body":"I think vertex lighting was resisted for several godot 4 versions and was not in 4.0 ","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3655490172/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3657410882","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/114021#issuecomment-3657410882","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/114021","id":3657410882,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7Z_6lC","user":{"login":"clayjohn","id":16521339,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTIxMzM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16521339?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn","html_url":"https://github.com/clayjohn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-12-15T20:14:59Z","updated_at":"2025-12-15T20:14:59Z","body":"See the discussion here: https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/78104\r\n\r\nMy preference would be to add the noperspective mode to varyings in the Godot Shader Language so users can use it in custom shaders. My sense is that most people doing PSX shaders go for the full aesthetic (crunchy textures, vertex snapping, affine texture mapping, dithering, etc.). So just adding affine texture mapping won't be enough. If we add noperspective, then anyone can easily use it and the code in BaseMaterial would become extremely simple","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3657410882/reactions","total_count":4,"+1":4,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3657602442","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/114021#issuecomment-3657602442","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/114021","id":3657602442,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7aApWK","user":{"login":"shittyprogrammer445","id":96263419,"node_id":"U_kgDOBbzc-w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96263419?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/shittyprogrammer445","html_url":"https://github.com/shittyprogrammer445","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shittyprogrammer445/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shittyprogrammer445/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shittyprogrammer445/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shittyprogrammer445/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shittyprogrammer445/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shittyprogrammer445/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shittyprogrammer445/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shittyprogrammer445/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shittyprogrammer445/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-12-15T21:06:07Z","updated_at":"2025-12-15T21:06:07Z","body":"> See the discussion here: #78104\r\n> \r\n> My preference would be to add the noperspective mode to varyings in the Godot Shader Language so users can use it in custom shaders. My sense is that most people doing PSX shaders go for the full aesthetic (crunchy textures, vertex snapping, affine texture mapping, dithering, etc.). So just adding affine texture mapping won't be enough. If we add noperspective, then anyone can easily use it and the code in BaseMaterial would become extremely simple\r\n\r\nI do agree that this would be a good change and one I'm willing to make, however would it even be possible to modify the shader compiler to do such a thing on low end hardware? I'm not familiar with how the shader compiler works so I can't say. I will try to get something working, and come back when I do.","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3657602442/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3658537567","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/114021#issuecomment-3658537567","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/114021","id":3658537567,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7aENpf","user":{"login":"shittyprogrammer445","id":96263419,"node_id":"U_kgDOBbzc-w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96263419?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/shittyprogrammer445","html_url":"https://github.com/shittyprogrammer445","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shittyprogrammer445/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shittyprogrammer445/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shittyprogrammer445/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shittyprogrammer445/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shittyprogrammer445/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shittyprogrammer445/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shittyprogrammer445/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shittyprogrammer445/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shittyprogrammer445/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-12-16T03:11:26Z","updated_at":"2025-12-16T03:28:38Z","body":"After a few hours of work, I was able to hack in support for `noperspective` on all rendering targets. The `gl_compatibility` renderer uses a similar technique to what this PR does to BaseMaterial3D, however it modifies the GLSL output instead of doing it in glslang. `mobile` and `forward_plus` use the `noperspective` keyword inside of GLSL. I'm unsure if I should commit this change to this PR or make another one, as this changes the fundamental purpose of the PR.\r\n\r\nGuidance would be appreciated, for now I'll keep the changes local and await further instructions.","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3658537567/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3658723903","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/114021#issuecomment-3658723903","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/114021","id":3658723903,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7aE7I_","user":{"login":"clayjohn","id":16521339,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTIxMzM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16521339?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn","html_url":"https://github.com/clayjohn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-12-16T04:24:10Z","updated_at":"2025-12-16T04:24:10Z","body":"Feel free to add it to this PR","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3658723903/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3659276119","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/114021#issuecomment-3659276119","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/114021","id":3659276119,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7aHB9X","user":{"login":"coobenguy","id":76452238,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc2NDUyMjM4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/76452238?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coobenguy","html_url":"https://github.com/coobenguy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coobenguy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coobenguy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coobenguy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coobenguy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coobenguy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coobenguy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coobenguy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coobenguy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coobenguy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-12-16T08:00:21Z","updated_at":"2025-12-16T08:00:21Z","body":"> Adding vertex lighting is also considered a rendering degradation, but this did not prevent it from becoming part of Godot.\r\n\r\nI would push against this, vertex shading is great for performance needs and things of that nature while affine is purely for stylization","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3659276119/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":1,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3660310539","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/114021#issuecomment-3660310539","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/114021","id":3660310539,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7aK-gL","user":{"login":"shittyprogrammer445","id":96263419,"node_id":"U_kgDOBbzc-w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96263419?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/shittyprogrammer445","html_url":"https://github.com/shittyprogrammer445","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shittyprogrammer445/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shittyprogrammer445/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shittyprogrammer445/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shittyprogrammer445/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shittyprogrammer445/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shittyprogrammer445/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shittyprogrammer445/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shittyprogrammer445/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shittyprogrammer445/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-12-16T12:33:26Z","updated_at":"2025-12-16T12:35:35Z","body":"> > Adding vertex lighting is also considered a rendering degradation, but this did not prevent it from becoming part of Godot.\n> \n> \n> \n> I would push against this, vertex shading is great for performance needs and things of that nature while affine is purely for stylization\n\nToon shading is also for stylization. I don't see the need to remove it now that it has a much better implementation. We have also assumed that StandardMaterial3D is supposed to just be for high quality rendering, but according to the Godot Documentation for BaseMaterial3D, \"This class serves as a default material with a wide variety of rendering features and properties without the need to write shader code.\"\n\nAdding this option to use 'noperspective' for the UV fits with this definition, as it's an abstraction of a core shader feature. A better shader abstraction might be an 'enum' of 'flat', 'smooth', and 'noperspective' interpolation modes but for now I believe just having the affine boolean is good enough ","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3660310539/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]